    {
      "id": "text-4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The first time I stepped out of the subway station, I think I understood John Green when he wrote TFIO. The twinkling lights, the cobbled streets, the walkability of it all, were lovely. (Plus, do you see how picturesque those clouds are?) \n\nAfter locating Miffy, she walked around with me to various museums, a few bars, and tastings of different cheeses, bitterballen, and more. She thought the Anne Frank house was the coolest."
    },
